WEBVTT

00:39:28.250 --> 00:39:31.768
And that's not, you know,
that is also back to the power thing.

00:39:31.792 --> 00:39:33.059
AG: Yes.

00:39:33.083 --> 00:39:36.601
EP: You know, it's like, why is one person
living the threat of loss here?

00:39:36.625 --> 00:39:38.833
And where is the other one?

00:39:39.417 --> 00:39:41.768
AG: Yeah. So I guess on that,

00:39:41.792 --> 00:39:44.184
I feel like, as a recovering
people pleaser,

00:39:44.208 --> 00:39:47.559
I've tried to overcome
some of these tendencies.

00:39:47.583 --> 00:39:50.601
Some of that came
from being trained as a negotiator

00:39:50.625 --> 00:39:52.184
and then teaching negotiation.

00:39:52.208 --> 00:39:55.309
Some of that came from learning
to do conflict mediation.

00:39:55.333 --> 00:39:59.976
A lot of it has come from just ending up
with an accumulating number of requests

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:02.309
where I just can't say no
to all of them anymore.